# Settings config panels

`RowFormWidget` is the shared form. Do not invent a panel base class or merge SkyLines / LiveTrack24 / Cloud / WeGlide.

## Dependent rows: collapse, do not leave gaps

`SetRowVisible` hides the control but **still reserves layout space**. Inapplicable children must use **`SetRowAvailable`** so the row leaves the layout (same as Expert via `SetExpertRow`).

```cpp
// BAD: blank hole when the parent is off
SetRowVisible(TRAIL_DRIFT, trail_on);

// GOOD
SetRowAvailable(TRAIL_DRIFT, trail_on);
```

Use **`SetRowEnabled`** (grey-out) for a **master enable** whose children still apply once on (credentials, intervals). Use **collapse** when the child does not apply (trail type when trail is Off).

**`AddDummy()`** is only for **ControlIndex alignment** when a row is not created on this platform (no rotate, no colour). Do not dummy-out parent-hidden children.

## Hide in the UI is not ignore at runtime

The profile still stores the child. The engine must key off the **parent**, or the child must stay visible.

Before collapsing a row, grep the setting. If it is still used for something else, **keep the row** and say so in help — do not change flight behaviour to match the menu.

| Pattern | Do |
|---|---|
| Child only used when parent is on | Collapse; confirm the parent guard in code |
| Dual-use (e.g. Reach polar → abort; Trail drift → circling track) | Keep visible (or always show); extend help/manual |

Expert-only rows are still applied; Expert is not a parent switch.

## Translatable enums and helpers

Translate the **unit**, not every numeric label (`_("%u sec")`, `_("%u min")`), matching `_("%u dpi")`.

Put `_()` / fill logic in a **`.cpp` already in `XCSOAR_SOURCES`**. Do not put gettext in a header (that needs a `gettext.mk` exception). Share a small row helper (e.g. `AddTrackingIntervalRow`) rather than copying AddEnum + fill + `RefreshDisplay`.

## Commits

One panel or one concern per commit. Fold immediate polish (helper extract, help text for the same row) into that feature; do not leave a fixup commit that only relocates the same change.
